<!-- =========================================================
     PAGE: ABOUT
========================================================= -->
<div class="page" id="page-about">
  <div class="breadcrumb"><div class="wrap"><button onclick="gotoPage('home')">Home</button> / About</div></div>

  <section class="hero" style="padding:64px 0 56px;">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="hero-eyebrow">Our Story</div>
      <h2 style="font-size:44px; max-width:18ch;">Why <em>engineering first</em> is a business model, not a slogan.</h2>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 360px; gap:72px; align-items:start;">
        <div class="narrative">
          <p>Most telecom hardware companies start with a product catalogue and work backwards to a story. Saga started differently: with a thesis about what clients in this market actually need, and why most vendors aren't able to deliver it.</p>

          <p>The thesis is straightforward. Enterprise and carrier-edge switch buyers don't just need a box that passes traffic. They need a platform they can build on — firmware they can customize, a supply chain they can rely on when allocation gets tight, and a technical relationship that doesn't reset every time they launch a new product generation.</p>

          <div class="pull-quote">"We're not a marketing-driven company. We put resources into engineering and inventory because that's where we actually create value for clients."</div>

          <p>That means we focus on two chipset ecosystems — Marvell Prestera for access-layer switching, CENTEC for aggregation, core, and data center — and we go deep on both. We optimize feature sets continuously. We hold strategic buffer stock on key chipsets. We do firmware and management UI customization at a depth most suppliers won't touch.</p>

          <p>The trade-off is transparency: we don't compete on every deal, and we're not the right partner for every buyer. We work best with clients who are optimizing for total cost of deployment, architectural consistency, and long-term supply predictability — not whoever quotes the lowest unit price this quarter.</p>

          <p>Saga is based in Shenzhen. We work with OEM and ODM clients, system integrators, ISPs, and distributors across global markets. Our relationships are built to last, and we take the long view on every account we pursue.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="identity-panel">
            <div class="panel-label">Company Profile</div>
            <div class="id-line">
              <span class="id-key">Base</span>
              <span class="id-val">Shenzhen, China</span>
            </div>
            <div class="id-line">
              <span class="id-key">Business Model</span>
              <span class="id-val">Engineering-led trade &amp; customization</span>
            </div>
            <div class="id-line">
              <span class="id-key">Chipset Focus</span>
              <span class="id-val">Marvell &middot; CENTEC &middot; Realtek</span>
            </div>
            <div class="id-line">
              <span class="id-key">Customization Depth</span>
              <span class="id-val">Hardware &middot; Firmware &middot; Management UI</span>
            </div>
            <div class="id-line">
              <span class="id-key">Supply Model</span>
              <span class="id-val">Strategic buffer stock</span>
            </div>
            <div class="id-line">
              <span class="id-key">Target Segments</span>
              <span class="id-val">OEM / ODM &middot; SIs &middot; ISPs &middot; Distributors</span>
            </div>
            <div class="id-line">
              <span class="id-key">Certifications</span>
              <span class="id-val">CE &middot; FCC &middot; RoHS &middot; REACH &middot; UKCA</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SUPPLY CHAIN -->
  <section class="section tight">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div>
          <div class="section-tag">Supply Chain</div>
          <h3>We manage uncertainty so you don't have to.</h3>
        </div>
        <p class="section-note">Strategic inventory isn't a cost center. It's the product.</p>
      </div>
      <p class="lead-text" style="margin-bottom:32px;">When chipset allocation tightens, our clients ship on schedule while others wait months. That reliability has a real dollar value that unit price comparisons don't capture.</p>
      <div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr); gap:0; border:1.5px solid var(--ink);">
        <div style="padding:26px; border-right:1.5px solid var(--ink); border-bottom:1.5px solid var(--ink);">
          <div class="section-tag" style="margin-bottom:8px;">Strategic Inventory</div>
          <p style="font-size:14px; color:#444; line-height:1.6;">Buffer stock held against key Marvell and CENTEC chipsets. Not speculative — planned against client demand forecasts and lifecycle position of each platform.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="padding:26px; border-bottom:1.5px solid var(--ink);">
          <div class="section-tag" style="margin-bottom:8px;">Lifecycle Planning</div>
          <p style="font-size:14px; color:#444; line-height:1.6;">We track chipset lifecycle status actively. Clients are informed well ahead of EOL transitions so product roadmaps can be adjusted without emergency re-spins.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="padding:26px; border-right:1.5px solid var(--ink);">
          <div class="section-tag" style="margin-bottom:8px;">Fast Lead Time</div>
          <p style="font-size:14px; color:#444; line-height:1.6;">Inventory on hand means orders move quickly. For standard configurations, lead times are materially shorter than going direct to factory without buffer stock in place.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="padding:26px;">
          <div class="section-tag" style="margin-bottom:8px;">Shortage Risk Mitigation</div>
          <p style="font-size:14px; color:#444; line-height:1.6;">Global chip shortages hit unprepared supply chains hard. Our inventory position is the hedge against that — built deliberately over time, not scrambled for at spot-market prices.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- WHAT WE DO AND DON'T -->
  <section class="section tight">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div>
          <div class="section-tag">Scope</div>
          <h3>What we do — and what we don't.</h3>
        </div>
        <p class="section-note">Clarity about scope saves everyone's time, including ours.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="boundary-grid">
        <div class="boundary-col">
          <h5>We Do</h5>
          <ul class="dash-list">
            <li>Access-layer switching — Marvell Prestera (L2+)</li>
            <li>Aggregation / core / data center — CENTEC (L3, 10G–800G)</li>
            <li>PoE / PoE+ / PoE++ commercial &amp; industrial</li>
            <li>OEM, ODM, SKD, CKD customization</li>
            <li>Deep firmware &amp; management UI customization</li>
            <li>Strategic chip inventory management</li>
            <li>CE &middot; FCC &middot; RoHS &middot; REACH &middot; UKCA certified products</li>
            <li>Long-term technical pre- and post-sales support</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="boundary-col">
          <h5>We Don't</h5>
          <ul class="dash-list dim">
            <li>Cloud-managed switching platforms</li>
            <li>Rail / transit certified switches (EN50155 etc.)</li>
            <li>IP67 ruggedized enclosures</li>
            <li>Consumer / home routers</li>
            <li>UL certification — not stocked as standard; available on request for qualified projects</li>
            <li>Country-specific mandatory certifications (KC, etc.) — not standard; available on request</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

